Well, if a dreamlike room appears at the hotel.
at least something, because it’s not about buying a better house
Morgan Stanley provides her capital for MUFG
Morgan Stanley announced Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group’s (MUFG) entry into her company, making this the first bank in Japan to spend nine billion dollars and thus take over 21% of its capital, an innovation due to a strong fall in its stock market price.
A week after a preliminary settlement was made public, the two banks stated that MUFG will buy 9.9% of Morgan Stanley common shares at a uniform price of $25.25, resulting in a total amount of $3 billion.
The assumed price is below 19% of the stock's price value from August 31.
MUFG will invest an additional $6 billion in the acquisition of convertible shares, which will secure a profit of 10% and resold at a cost of $31.25.
Morgan Stanley explained that the global business will be done on the basis of a unified average price of $29, i.e. 28% above the current price value.
Morgan Stanley shares, however, fell 6.79% to $23.07 at 17.00 GMT.
“This strategic connection represents an important opportunity to accelerate Morgan Stanley’s transition to the status of a holding bank,” said John Mack, Director General of the American Group.
Morgan Stanley adopted this status last week, which is supposed to allow it to expand its businesses to new areas, but under the supervision of the Federal Reserve.
Their association with MUFG also confirms that the current financial crisis is forcinging Wall Street's biggest names to take a much more cautious stance than before.
The modalities presented on Monday also show that the agreement has changed over the course of the last few days: Last Monday, Morgan had simply declared that it would sell up to 20% of its shares for about $8.5 billion to Japan.
`A week agove,' declared in Tokyo Toshihide Mizuno, managing director of MUFG, `we thought the stake would consist entirely of common shares.
But given the current economic and market situation, we wanted to reduce the risks and protect ourselves.”
Based on a balanced average price, MUFG will pay 7% for its Morgan Stanley shares below their price value.
And the business is going to take place with a reduction in profit by about 20% per share.
The agreement that MUFG will be able to convert half of its preferred shares into common shares in one year if the latter are exchanged more than 50% above the sale value within a given period, i.e. at approximately $47.
Morgan Stanley assures that the funds supplied by MUFG will allow him to use investment opportunities, strengthen their balance sheet and increase their sales.
However, a spokesman for the group refused to provide more detailed information on the strategic plans of the two new allies.
Following MUFG's investment, Morgan Stanley should be able to post a solvency rate of approximately 15%, one of the best in this sector.
Morgan said it had 'significantly lowered its balance sheet since the end of August.
The past few weeks have been tough for the group, which had to watch its stock market price fall by half, while the price for insurance against default skyrocketed.
This price declined on Monday but remained at a high level, at about 12%.
Goldman Sachs, the only other 'survivors' of the big investment banks on Wall Street following the bankruptcy of Bear Stearns and Lehman Brothers and the acquisition of Merrill Lynch, announced last week that it had withdrawn $15 billion, in part at Berkshire Hathaway, Warren Buffett's group.
Rafael Correa this Monday in Quito.
re-founding the republic around 21st-century socialism.
This is the joint project of the Venezuelan Hugo Chávez, the Bolivian Evo Morales and the Equatorian Rafael Correa.
It was the third party who this Sunday, following the example of his like-minders and friends, put up for election the plan of a new constitution.
Mission accomplished, because according to 80% of the electoral vote, 64% voted `yes' in the referendum.
According to these results, 28% voted `no', 7% of the ballot papers were invalid and 0.7% were delivered empty.
In order for the constitutional project to be passed, one vote must be scored more than half of all votes cast.
On Sunday, two polls conducted at the exits of polling stations and a counting of a non-governmental organization had announced a clear victory for 'yes', prophesiging 63% to 70%.
By the way, on the night from Sunday to Monday, Rafael Correa had demanded the victory of his constitutional project.
The ‘constitution has triumphed overwhelmingly,’ he had assured Guayaquil, the government’s seat 280 kilometers southwest of Quito and congratulated the Equatorians.
Of course Rafael Correa was congratulated by Chávez and Morales, but also by his Chilean like-minded Michelle Bachelet.
The election, which was quietly held according to the observational delegation of the Organization of American States (OAS), referred to a 444-point text to secure the `new socialism', for which the President advocates.
The constitutional project transfers state power to the economy by giving it the sole right to 'development planning' in a country that largely thrives on petroleum production by foreign companies and from the foreign exchange that emigrates send into the country.
The project, which will be pushed by Correa elected in 2006, will also allow the head of state broader power, who will be ablove up to two consecutive mandates of four years each, and will have the opportunity to dissolve the National Assembly.
Correa has already announced that he will make use of this power and seek a new mandate in February 2009.
The Constitution also ensures the principle of free medical care and education that the president has already begun to introduce in this country with 13.9 million inhabitants, where 50% of the population lives below the poverty line.
In the end, it also envisags prohibiting the presence of foreign troops, which will put an end to the agreement between Quito and Washington to use an equatorian base as a starting station for American anti-drug operations.
The 19 hostages were liberated in Chad
An Egyptian commando launched the attack on the kidnappers of the eleven tourists and their eight companions, who had been captured ten days ago.
You're in Cairo.
The eleven European tourists and their eight Egyptian companions, who were held captives in the desert for eleven days, were returned to the Egyptian capital this Monday afternoon healthy and unscathed.
In the morning they had been liberated by an Egyptian command in Chad.
Seemingly in good condition, the hostages arrived at around 15.30 on board a special aircraft the al-Maza military base right next to Cairo's international airport.
They were taken directly, without being able to speak to the press, on board a helicopter to the hospital of Maadi, a foreigner's district of Cairo, to be examined there.
They enjoy all `best health' and the kidnappers `was not paid a ransom', explained Egyptian Tourism Minister Zoheir Garanna on the tarcock.
After being captured on September 19 in an SUV safari at the foot of Mount Ouanat in the border area of Egypt, Sudan and Libya, the group of hostages was repeatedly taken by 35 unknown kidnappers from one hideout to the next.
There are eleven tourists - five Italians, five Germans and one Romanian - and also eight Egyptians: two guides, four chauffeurs, a border keeper, and the director of the Aegypty Agency, organizer of the safari.
An Egyptian security official explained that 30 members of the special forces, from board two helicopters, launched the attack at night, just before dawn.
`On both sides, shots were fired and half of the kidnappers were killed, the rest fleded," said this official, who wishes to remain anonymous.
He explained that a total of 150 members of Egypt's special forces had been sent to Sudan, where they received support from German and Italian commandos.
The head of Italian diplomat Franco Frattini reported from Belgrade, where he is currently, about the role played by secret agents and elements of the Italian special forces.
"We have to acknowledge that, thanks to the professionalism and performance of our men from the secret service and special forces," he explained without further details.
He also denied that a ransom had been paid.
The night before, the Sudanese army had claimed to have stopped during a patrol an all-terrain vehicle in which the kidnappers were located, of which they killed six, including the Chad-born leader, and two arrests.
The army stated that they were connected to a rebel group from Darfour, the Libération du Soudan-Unité (SLA-U) movement, which, however, denied this movement immediately.
Letters - The silent majority of culture
A debate on funding the culture is making headlines and is the central theme of the current election campaign.
The better.
But one area of our cultural life continues to be forgotten.
Who will stand up and denounce the pathetic sums granted to the small museums, archives, archaeological excavations or the national historical sites that starve miserably?
Which politician will dare to remind the federal government that it neglects its monuments and its culturally significant buildings?
That there are no proper laws in Quebec, as well as in Canada, which effectively protect our cultural heritage?
Did you know that the French government provides 3.5 million euros solely for the restoration of Chinon Castle in the Loire Valley?
Among our American neighbors, it is written in their country's constitution that the protection of cultural heritage belongs to the culture of the American, and that this cultural heritage must be protected by all citizens, all deputies, in mutual coordination.
In Quebec, in the Association of History Societies of Quebec, at least 40,000 volunteers gathered in 211 historical societies strive to deal intensively with history, with a few pennies to save the numerous private archives, and preserve the archaeological remnants.
They are also often the watchdogs of our cultural heritage, who protest with the power of desperation when promoters and decision-makers release their bulldozers to our old stones and forgotten cemeteries.
When will there be a stage for history and cultural heritage?
Benelux governments nationalize parts of Fortis Bank
With partial nationalization, the Benelux countries want to support the Belgian-Dutch Fortis Bank caused by the US financial crisis: The three states provide a total of EUR 11.2 billion to the banking and insurance institution, which also has branches in Hungary.
The governments of Belgium, Luxembourg and the Netherlands discussed this weekend at the highest level, together with the President of the European Central Bank and the representative of the competition authority of the European Commission.
In the eurozone, Fortis is the first victim of the international financial market crisis, which has been ongoing in a year, so decisions now being made in connection with the bank could have a precedent.
In accordance with the decision made on Sunday night, all three states buy the respective shares of the bank at about 49 percent.
The bank will presumably sell part of its holdings, notable the insurance activities bought by the Dutch ABN Amro last year.
Forti's shares began a steep descent last week, in the second half of the week, serious crisis scenarios were already emerging.
However, analysts agree that the bank, with its 85,000 employees, is far too big for a bankruptcy.
The institute's securities fell 12% to a 14-year low on Friday.
Since January, the value of shares fell by more than two-thirds.
In view of the current share prices, the market value of the group amounts to EUR 14 billion, which is unrealistic according to the management.
According to management, the $700 billion American bailout and the resulting uncertainty in the markets is to blame for the downturn of Fortis shares.
However, prices rose slightly on Monday.
On Friday, Filip Dierckx was appointed as the bank's new director-general.
The financial institution was also looking for a private buyer, but there has been no prospect with a factual offer.
The Belgian government, meanwhile, has sought reassurance - no investor is said to tremble for his money, it said.
So far, there has been no panic among the customers, the branches of the bank have not been stormed.
In Hungary, Fortis has its own branches, but it also owns leasing companies.
Fox in chicken coop
Due to a person’s medication consumption, life and health insurance companies often refuse to enter into a contract with a customer.
Data protection experts fear the data market could become uncontrollable.
“There are data protection programs that in any case links the use of the drug data to the consent of the data subject.
These should be independent hands, otherwise we entrust the fox's chickens," the Washington Post quotes Richard Dick, developer of the prescribing data tracking program.
Insurancies determine the fees as well as the payment amounts in the event of damage depending on the health status of the customer, and if the risk is estimated too high, the insurance is not taken out in the first place.
Previously, the customer was sent for a medical examination, and the contract was concluded only in knowledge of the results.
Ten years ago Dick invented a far more favorable method: Based on the identification number of the customer, he obtains the data of the last one and a half years from the pharmacies, i.e. which preparations were bought, and the program calculates from which disease the customer suffers from and what his state of health is.
For example, if he regularly buys large amounts of cholesterol-lowering drugs, it could be concluded that his blood lipid levels are untreatably high, which would automatically place him in a higher risk group.
There are several versions of the program in circulation - some even define a risk multiplier, so the insurance companies only have to do the paperwork, but there are minor difficulties.
One of the disadvantages is that many medications can be taken for various purposes, such as migraines and hot flashes, but also against depression.
From the point of view of insurers, the latter is a high-risk factor, while those mentioned before.
For querying and processing the data, their own companies have formed, which, before they obtain the data, ask the patient for his consent.
In the meantime, they have to do so by law, although omissions have not yet been punished.
Some companies even process the results of laboratory examinations and connect them with the data on drug use, providing an even more accurate picture of the health status of patients.
More and more companies have access to the data, and at the same time controlling their use is becoming more difficult.
Although there is a separate data protection law for health data, its effect extends only to service providers in the health sector and insurance companies.
The bill has already been submitted to Congress, according to which authorities could also control data processing firms.
Dick Richard sees that this is too little, so he wants to further develop his program, so that the data can only be passed on with the consent of the person concerned.
Another question, of course, is that the data subject can hardly prohibit access to his data, otherwise the insurance companies do not conclude a contract with him.
And so the chickens are left to the grace of the fox.
General meal plan from Marseille
European Union and India double trade
Since the European Union and India are each other's leading trading partners on both sides, this was the main issue alongside other global problems at the ninth summit.
Today the French-Indian summit will also take place, which will mainly discuss cooperation in the nuclear energy sector.
Although the European Union recognizes that India is an emerging, democratic major power that should be given more voices and a say on international concerns, the member states have not yet been able to agree on whether or not they should support New Delhi's permanent membership in the UN Security Council.
This question was not discussed at yesterday's ninth summit in Marseille yesterday.
French President and current European Council President Nicolas Sarkozy, as well as Commission President José Manuel Barroso and chief diplomat Javier Solana received Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh. An agreement has been reached that trade will double over the next five years, i.e. to a good €100 billion.
Given the fact that the exchange of goods had risen from 25 to 55 billion between 2000 and 2007, this target is not so ambitious.
In this sense, the 26 existing civil flight agreements with India have also been legally combined into an agreement, so that in the future air transport will also be boosted.
By 2009, India intends to sign the free trade agreement with the Union.
Sarkozy pledged to speed up the pact.
The aim is to strike a balance in the currently unbalanced relationship between the EU and India: while the Union is the number one partner of India, New Delhi ranks only ninth among EU partners.
The summit was devoted to global concerns.
Among them was the situation in Afghanistan and Pakistan, or the terrorism that both sides condemned in the strongest possible terms. The convening of a UN conference was also urged.
The Doha round should also be completed, with both sides to blame for the failure.
The EU stressed that it is sticking to its energy and climate programme, i.e. pollutant emissions are to be reduced by at least 20% by 2020.
India also agreed with this, as well as with the proposal to make a kind of global compromise at the upcoming climate summit and to reduce greenhouse gas production by 50 percent by 2050.
The rise in the price of food should also be combated, which is why both support the convening of an international conference on the subject of the financial crisis.
The Indian head of government visits the French capital today, where he will sign an agreement on the peaceful use of nuclear energy at a bilateral meeting.
In Paris, however, one hopes for orders to French companies worth EUR 20 billion for the construction of nuclear reactors in India.
According to agency reports, the agreement is to be adopted for 15 years.
Over 300 Italian publishers in Frankfurt
Strong presence of Italian publishers at the International Frankfurt Book Fair.
More than 300 Italian publishers will be present at the 60th book fair, the most important international event for the acquisition of rights.
The international Frankfurt book fair expects more than 7,000 exhibitors from 101 countries for the current event. They will spread over the 171,790 square meters of the fair and present over 403,000 titles. Turkey will be the guest of honor of the event.
Maria Giro will represent the Italian government during the opening ceremony in the exhibition hall: Italy will be representing the 264 sqm "Punto Italia" exhibition space.
This will be followed by a press conference near the room structure in the exhibition hall 5.0 of the book fair: on this occasion, digits, trends and perspectives around publishing in Italy will be discussed.
According to the data, the importance of books by foreign writers decreases throughout, but in particular in the adult and youth division.
Billionaire Steve Fossett's small aircraft, which disappeared a year ago
Steve Fossett's small plane, the billionaire who disappeared on September 3, 2007 on a flight over the Nevada desert, has been founded.
The individual parts have been found on a high plateau of 3000 m, in the area of the Sierra Nevada Mammoth Lakes between the states of California and Nevada.
However, there were no human remains inside the aircraft.
Madera County Sheriff, John Anderson, completely invalidated the final doubts during a press conference: "The plane has been localized, whereupon a force was sent out. Now we have the assurance that it was the plane that Steve Fossett flew on the day of his disappearance."
Mr. Anderson also further confirmed that no human remains were found on the plane or its proximity.
The 63-year-old billionaire was pronounced dead in February.
The U.S. Office for Road Safety (Ntsb) noted that just a few hours after sighting of the plane, a crew was dispatched that identified the plane: the Bellanca 8kcab, which was lost on September 3, 2007, after Fossett in Yerington in Nevada for a 3-hour flight.
Finally, some of Fossett's personal belongings were also found in California, not far neighboring the Nevada border from a couple near their home on Mammoth Lakes.
These are two badges with the name Fossetts, both of which had been issued by the Federal Aviational Administration of illinois, cash and a jacket.
The search for Fossett had been abandoned a month after his disappearance.
The billionaire had conquered a place in history through a long sequence of records.
In 2002, in the sixth attempt, he became the first person to circle the world ball in a hot air balloon: a two-week, solitary flight.
Three years later, he flew around the world in a sintle flight without a stopover with an aircraft.
Among his several records also includes a flight of 15445 m over the Andes, but this with a co-pilot.
Glk, the advertising you're not expecting
A suv that, due to its original design and special lines, the expansive surface and its clear angles, falls out of the conventional schemes.
Mercedes-Benz has tried with this off-roader to breathe new breath into the sector.
Due to its extraordinary characteristics, the presentation of the Suv Glk will also be unconventional, which will be on display in the Mercedes-Benz showroom from 17 October.
Thus, the advertising drum that will accompany the appearance of the new model will also appear in a new dress, namely in the form of a 3D campaign – a novelty in the car sector in backward Italy.
A project with a maximum effort that will be carried out in various chamfers that will occupy Milan’s central shopping mile, the Corso Como, until 15 November.
The first chamfer will consist of the presentation of the car in form, whereby 3D glasses, which are distributed near the Corso Como, are intended to give the whole a special look: the new Suv will thus appear in its almost real dimensions as a three-dimensional model.
In fact, the car will thus seemingly emerge from the poster on which it is pictured.
With the help of the Elumina8 technology, the new Glk is illuminated at different moments in all its details in order to re-assemble as a whole.
Undoubtedly, the concern of Mercedes with this advertising is to introduce a new kind of author’s record into this rather stereotypical field.
However, will it be possible to irritate the interest of the future buyers? We will see it.
Now it's clear who the Italian hooligans are
They come from the Triveneto – now they risk stadium ban
Who are these 150-200 boys and girls, for whom the whole of Italy is now ashamed? They are part of the "Ultras Italia" group, which has been travelling behind the Italian national team for years and which, honestly, did not cause any serious problems until recently.
There have never been clashes with opposing fans so far.
The origin of the group lies in the right milieu.
The promoters come from the Triveneto.
From Verona, Padova, Trieste and Udine.
Other smaller groups from Campania and Puglia joined them in Sofia.
They wear the tricolori, on which the cities of the militants appear: these, however, were removed on Saturday to avoid identification.
Their role models are the English fans.
In Bulgaria there was now a clash with a truly right-wing fan scene, that of Levski.
From Figc, 144 tickets had been provided to the Italian fans for the game: all were exhibited in names and thus easy to control.
In fact, they were also all controlled by the Viminal: among those traveled to Sofia, no one with an ongoing stadium-prohibition procedure.
Four fans of the Italian team, who were already burdened in this regard, were also denied the ticket and the trip to Bulgaria.
Now the Viminal is awaiting the reports of the Bulgarian police to take further steps: in this case Tifosi arrested or identified in the riots can expect a stadium ban of at least five years.
This is an international ban that prevents access to stadiums across Europe.
Our hooligans will no longer set foot in a stadium.
Luckily.
But now, of course, there is afraid of imitation offenders, who could follow them little more than 150.
"This fire must be leaked immediately, and that in no case give such behavior the opportunity for justification," according to the Viminal.
Therefore, "eyes on especially with regard to Wednesday's national team's game in Lecce."
In fact, there is a small core of Italian ultras in Puglia.
Tomorrow, the Osservatorio (Sports Supervision) gathers, on Tuesday the Casms, which can count on a part of the Aise, i.e. the secret services that deals with the problem of stadium violence.
"Duce-Duce shouts and the raised right arm during Mameli's hymn? In Bulgaria, this is not a criminal offence..."
This is the idea of Domenico Mazzilli (significantly expressed without joy), who has been the director of Osservatorio at the Viminal for a few weeks (he took the post of Francensco Tagliente and Felice Ferlizzi on it).
Mazzilli was the police president of Trieste, where a nucleus of the supporters of Ultras Italia, founded in 2002.
It is true, says Mazzilli, that in Bulgaria it is not opposed to the law to praise the Duce, but without a doubt the behavior of these 150-200 people was a disgrace.
“I am not a sociologist—adds the #1 of the Osservatorio—crimes are punished in the land of their action.
Until now, this group had kept in check, but now it must be reconsidered what has happened and will happen.
But we are also talking about the whistles during Mameli's hymn: even this is not a criminal offence, but they allow me, there is a lack of parenting...".
